      "eyebrow": "The law",
      "heading": "What RIDDOR requires",
      "html": "<p>A dangerous occurrence is an event listed in Schedule 2. On construction sites that includes a crane or lifting appliance failing or overturning. It includes a scaffold collapse over five metres, any unplanned collapse of a building or structure, and a release of a dangerous biological agent.</p><p>The list is fixed. A near miss outside it is not a RIDDOR report. The Management Regulations 1999 still say you must control risks. RIDDOR records must be kept for at least three years.</p>"
